WEBVTT Kind: captions; Language: en

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.001
Music There miss, you see the heterodontists
are feeding back into the stimulus

00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:29.000
reaction activators causing non-snaps
of the motor control resistor units.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Oh that's good.

00:00:31.001 --> 00:00:33.000
No lady that's bad.

00:00:33.001 --> 00:00:36.001
But your regenerative circuits are
tuned asynchronously and that causes

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:39.000
concatenation in the intermediate amplifiers.

00:00:39.001 --> 00:00:41.000
Well that's bad isn't it?

00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:43.001
No that's good.

00:00:44.001 --> 00:00:47.000
From now on I don't think there will be
the slightest trouble with your robot.

00:00:47.001 --> 00:00:49.001
Your domestic problems are completely solved.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Well thank you very much.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.000
That's perfectly alright.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.001
And if there's anything else
you want to know about your

00:00:58.001 --> 00:01:00.000
robot don't hesitate to give us a ring.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Good day.

00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:14.000
Rolo answer the door.

00:01:31.001 --> 00:01:36.001
Time here.

00:02:07.001 --> 00:02:10.000
[...]

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.001
[...]

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.001
Music Yes ma'am.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.001
Rolo get.

00:02:35.001 --> 00:03:00.001
[...]

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Music Yes Rolo the robot.

00:03:13.001 --> 00:03:17.000
The chromium plated butler is
just a daydream after all.

00:03:18.001 --> 00:03:21.000
But not so Rolo's little
brother and sister robots.

00:03:21.001 --> 00:03:25.001
The millions of small mechanical servants
that never ask for afternoons off.

00:03:25.001 --> 00:03:30.000
The amazing machines and gadgets that
almost seem to think for themselves.

00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:38.000
The tiny clockwork brains and heat regulators
on our kitchen stoves apparently do

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.001
almost everything except read the cookbook.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Thinking machines like this keep
golden brown slices of toast from

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.001
turning into slabs of charcoal.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.000
And keep the coffee hot until
we're ready to start dunking.

00:03:51.001 --> 00:03:55.000
Then there's a tea kettle that's
been trained never to boil dry.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:59.000
When the water is gone the kettle simply
pulls out its own attachment plug.

00:04:00.001 --> 00:04:04.001
And here's a gadget that ought to read
a bow from every dog in the country.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.001
A Fido feeder that never forgets when
the puff is dining home alone and the

00:04:09.001 --> 00:04:11.000
rest of the family is dining out.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.001
What's more it tells him
when to come and get it.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.001
In offices and school rooms too,
robots have learned to turn on the lights.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:26.000
This little electric eye measures the
amount of daylight coming in the windows.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.000
When the light level outside drops below
the requirement for good visibility,

00:04:30.001 --> 00:04:34.001
this robot throws a switch and
the first bank of lights goes on.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.000
No robot machine has ever
been accused of being absent

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.000
minded or careless at its work.

00:04:42.001 --> 00:04:48.000
Here a robot that never sleeps nor winks
nor looks out the window stands guard

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.000
over the men who work at this giant press.

00:04:51.001 --> 00:04:56.001
As long as the robot can see the man,
the press won't budge an inch and that's

00:04:56.001 --> 00:04:58.001
mighty important on a big job like this.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.001
Did you ever hear of anyone getting
his lap caught in an elevator door?

00:05:04.001 --> 00:05:08.001
That can't happen here because as
long as there's anything in the way

00:05:08.001 --> 00:05:10.001
this door can't close.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:15.000
Step back please.
There's plenty of room in the rear of the car.

00:05:15.001 --> 00:05:20.000
All right then don't step back. Just take
a deep breath and hang on to yourself.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.001
One little robot, for example,
always remembers to serve drinks when it sees

00:05:28.001 --> 00:05:30.000
anyone walking around with a thirst.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.000
A beam of light is aimed across the
fountain and into an electric eye.

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:39.001
When the beam of light is broken by a
solid object such as this head, the

00:05:39.001 --> 00:05:43.000
electric eye control opens the
faucet and there's your drink.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.001
This particular device is an
automatic fire sprinkler.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.000
Someday maybe someone will invent
a robot that can take a joke.

00:05:53.001 --> 00:05:55.001
Some robots have even learned to fly.

00:05:57.001 --> 00:06:02.000
Tiny automatic brains in giant airliners,
sensitive to the slightest change in

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.001
balance or direction, relieve the busy
pilots of the job of keeping the wings

00:06:06.001 --> 00:06:10.001
level, the nose on the horizon,
and the plane headed in the right direction.

00:06:11.001 --> 00:06:15.001
Don't look now,
but this motor car is simply full of robots.

00:06:17.001 --> 00:06:23.000
In the carburetor is a diet specialist,
a brainy collection of jets and valves

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:27.001
and floats that serve a health menu of
gasoline calories and fresh air vitamins

00:06:27.001 --> 00:06:32.000
to the engine, a menu that varies
with every change in speed or load.

00:06:33.001 --> 00:06:38.000
The engine likes its meals served
not too hot and not too cold.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.000
So in the intake manifold, another mastermind
with a nervous system sensitive to

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.001
heat uses hot exhaust gases to warm the
mixture before it goes into the engine.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.001
Step right up close to the platform
and see the Siamese robots.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.001
These robots attached to the
distributor are always worrying

00:06:57.001 --> 00:06:59.000
about the spark in the engine.

00:07:00.001 --> 00:07:03.000
One is sure that the spark
ought to be advanced.

00:07:03.001 --> 00:07:07.000
The other is equally sure that it
ought to be retarded just a trifle.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.000
But they never argue.

00:07:09.001 --> 00:07:14.000
Each takes his turn according to the speed
and load, and between them they manage

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
to stage a grand performance
every time they go on the road.

00:07:18.001 --> 00:07:23.001
One little robot, a very small but
intelligent brain, sits up back of the engine

00:07:23.001 --> 00:07:28.000
in the voltage regulator and keeps close
tabs on the generator to see that the

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.001
generator makes enough current
to keep the battery fully

00:07:30.001 --> 00:07:32.001
charged, but not too full.

00:07:33.001 --> 00:07:37.000
And still another deep thinker
rides way up in front.

00:07:37.001 --> 00:07:42.000
Its job is to keep water from cooling
off in the radiator until the engine is

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.000
warmed up to a good working temperature.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:49.001
Then in the vacuum power gear shift,
there's a robot strongman who

00:07:49.001 --> 00:07:51.001
thrives on almost nothing at all.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.001
With a bit of a vacuum, this sturdy fellow
can almost shift for himself if we'll

00:07:58.001 --> 00:08:00.000
just tell him what we want him to do.

00:08:01.001 --> 00:08:05.001
Robots have even taken up the art
of dial twisting in our radios.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.000
All we need to do is push
the button and listen.

00:08:10.001 --> 00:08:14.001
Driving wouldn't be half so much fun
if we didn't have that phantom crew of

00:08:14.001 --> 00:08:16.001
intelligent robots to help us.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:22.000
Every day in our homes and offices,
as well as in our motor cars, hundreds of

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:26.001
these little robots are doing more things
for us than we realize, taking care of

00:08:26.001 --> 00:08:32.001
the routine tasks and leaving us free to
live and work and play in greater ease

00:08:32.001 --> 00:08:34.001
and comfort and safety.
